  "likelihood": "per parent interval i with n_i equal pieces of length D_i: d_i*log(1-(1-p_i)^n_i) + (1-d_i)*n_i*log(1-p_i), p_i = g(eta(x_i, D_i)). At n_i = 1 this is the Bernoulli likelihood of the published GLM arms; for the cloglog-offset arm the aggregation collapses to exp(-lambda*L) at every n_i, so that arm is grid-invariant by construction",
  "not_the_thing_this_replaces": "`--alloc uniform` in incident_grid_reframe.py writes each piece as a fractional 0/1 row pair, whose objective is prod_j p_j^(1/n)(1-p_j)^(1-1/n). That matches the event count and invents no date, but it is not the interval-censored likelihood 1 - prod_j(1 - p_j), which is what this script maximises",
