  "published_model_convergence": "the published primary model is sklearn LogisticRegression(C=1.0) at its default tol=1e-4, which stops after ~10 iterations. Re-running the IDENTICAL objective to tol=1e-10 changes the US predicted-to-observed ratio from 1.1606 to 1.1698 and the US AUROC by 3.6e-4; the unpenalised GLM arms of incident_cloglog.py sit at the converged value, which is why the L2 anchor here is gated against the converged reference and the published-row difference is reported as a disclosure. No manuscript conclusion turns on it (both values over-predict the US), but the published numbers are converged to 1e-4, not to machine precision.",
